MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_001: Ah, Promised One. You find me in a\ncontemplative mood.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_002: <NCA>"I thought you were dead."
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_003: <NCB>"You haven't been back for a few days."
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_004: Is that it?
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_005: <NCA>"Why stay away so long?"
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_006: I wonder, Promised One. How do you feel about\nthis fight?
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_007: For me, every day brought joy. I relished the battle\nagainst the risen dead.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_008: There are strong foes I never otherwise could have\nfaced, and worthy opponents I had not yet felled.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_009: Powerful ancients I should never have known have\nreturned to the fray. My soul trembled with it.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_010: But it could not last. I have grown accustomed to\nfighting them.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_011: I have lost count of my opponents, and with that the\nfights lost their savor.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_012: I anticipate their feints. I know the full measure of\ntheir skill. They do not learn. They do not change.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_013: Hm...
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_014: A true duel to the death can only be fought by\nthe living.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_015: I have grown weary of this world of corpses.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_016: Saying these things, I feel I disappoint her a\nsecond time... Heh.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_017: I suppose that willfulness is also why you were forced\nto seek me here.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_018: I passed many days felling foes without respite, until\nmy soul became dulled. It eases my thirst.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_019: <NCA>"It is time to rest."
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_020: <NCB>"Please, care more for your soul."
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_021: <ACA>First, you will quench my thirst.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_022: <ACB>Those words are familiar...but miss the mark. By\ndueling, I honor my soul!
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_023: Ah!
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_024: A jest, only. I know you are in no mood to duel\nme now.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_025: Your only concern is the world's salvation. I will\ncontinue to swat away the blades of the dead.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_026: <NCA>"Thank you for understanding."
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_027: I do not need thanks. Many whom I would duel\nyet live.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_A_028: We will end Balor, separate the land of the living\nfrom that of the dead, and I will have my duels then.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_001: Promised One?
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_002: <NCA>"Did you think I was dead?"
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_003: <NCB>"Feeling reflective again?"
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_004: <ACA>Hehe. No, I was not worried.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_005: <ACB>Hehe. Not today.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_006: I was considering you. You fascinate me.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_007: I came to this land by chance. I fought my way\nacross it in search of satisfaction.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_008: I had no interest in the fate of the world. Even were\nit to be extinguished.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_009: <NCA>"So why fight beside me?"
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_010: Because you were there.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_011: If you had not arrived, I think... Yes, inevitably,\nunable to bear my thirst, I would have left this land.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_012: I let myself get swept up into this foolhardy battle to\nsave the world.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_013: Yet I am pleased to have seen it through. Strange.\nLike you.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_014: <NCA>"It isn't over yet."
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_015: <NCB>"Will you accompany me?"
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_016: <ACA>Oh, so you mean to say that there are greater heights\nyet before us?
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_017: <ACB>Oh? You require my strength yet?
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_018: Hah.
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_019: Very well. I will stand beside you. But before that,\nwe duel!
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_020: Ngh...
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_021: <RSDS>Ah, yes. This is the way! This will satisfy me! My\nsoul is aflame!
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_022: Death comes to everyone. That is why we live, and\ntremble at life's beauty!
MID_SE_Ism_Dit_S_023: My dance will continue, and I will draw you into it!\nWe will dance together, Promised One!